{"type":"message","id":"bfd3f97b","parentId":"3675654f","timestamp":"2026-04-01T12:12:06.511Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I ran the pipeline again on the new image.\n\n**Kidney Cancer Detector**\n- **Kidney cancer class:** `kidney_normal`\n- **Confidence:** `0.9999996423721313`\n- **Inference time:** `2.3189 s`\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- **Image Analyzer prediction:** `kidney_normal`\n- **CAM coverage:** `0.015306122448979591`\n- **CAM center ratio:** `0.9999999997916666`\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** `0.04166666665798611`\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** `0.9999999997916666`\n- **CAM explanation:** The model focused on a localized central renal region in a way it considered compatible with normal kidney anatomy, without a pattern suggesting a localized abnormal lesion.\n\n**X-AI**\n- **Confidence interpretation:** The model was very confident in this prediction, but this still should not be treated as a confirmed medical diagnosis.\n- **Summary:** The pipeline did **not** support a definitive cancer finding from this image and described the kidney as appearing more consistent with a normal result.\n- **Visual evidence:** The image shows a kidney, but the explanation says there is not enough evidence here to define a specific pathology.\n- **Recommended next steps:**\n  1. Consult a medical professional for a proper evaluation.\n  2. Share the image and any relevant history for further review.\n\n**References**\n- National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases — https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/kidney-disease\n- American Kidney Fund — https://www.kidneyfund.org/kidney-disease/kidney-cancer\n\n**Important:** this pipeline output is a **preliminary signal, not an actual diagnosis**.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/9b207c57-61e2-4481-bfee-982fe497b3ce.jpg\n\nCompared with the previous image, this second run came back **normal**, while the first came back **kidney_tumor**. If you want, I can give you a **side-by-side comparison** of the two results.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0ed6dc373c5281050169cd0b8ca2f88191bca06dbb1bdb406a\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":9649,"output":507,"cacheRead":22144,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32300,"cost":{"input":0.0241225,"output":0.007605,"cacheRead":0.005536,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0372635}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775045515092}}
